Fixtures for the local campaign tests (synthetic; the MKL_VERBOSE lines follow the oneMKL version-line format
"MKL_VERBOSE oneMKL <ver> Update <u> Product build <date> for Intel(R) 64 architecture <ISA text> enabled processors,
Lnx <GHz> lp64 <threading layer>", with versions from the audit (SuperMUC stack/24.6.0: 2025.3; Helma preset: 2024.2.2).
The exact strings on the machines are unverified; the parser in provenance.sh (prov_mkl_parse) matches loosely.
sysfs/ is a fake /sys cpufreq tree (macOS has none); proc/self/maps lists a fake fakeintel library for the preload check.
info_*.txt / timers_*.txt: info lines in every N_delay format collect.py must parse, and the T1 timers.txt format.
